  "description": "Reid Bikes Tract Jr. 24 | 24\" Kids' mountain bike\nBuilt for young adventurers aged 9–11, the Reid Bikes Tract Jr. 24 is a kids' mountain bike designed for everything from neighbourhood rides to off-road adventures. With a tough yet lightweight alloy frame, front suspension, wide tyres and powerful cable disc brakes, it's built to give young riders confidence across a variety of terrain.\nThe alloy frame features increased step-over clearance for easier mounting and dismounting, while kids' specific aluminium components help keep the bike lightweight and easy to handle.\nThe 50mm front suspension helps keep bumps at bay, while double-wall alloy rims and wide 2.35\" tyres provide grip and stability on the trail. Shimano 7-speed Tourney gearing gives young riders a useful range for tackling changing terrain, while powerful cable disc brakes provide reliable control when things get more adventurous.\nWhether they're riding around the neighbourhood, exploring local trails or heading out with family and friends, the Reid Bikes Tract Jr. 24 is built to help young riders keep up, explore the outdoors and enjoy every ride.\nWho is the Reid Bikes Tract Jr. 24 for?\nThe Tract Jr. 24\" Kids' Mountain Bike is ideal for:\n\nYoung riders aged 9–11\nKids who want to explore neighbourhoods, parks and trails\nRiders looking for a tough but lightweight alloy mountain bike\nYoung cyclists who want 7-speed gearing\nRiders who want front suspension and wide tyres for varied terrain\nKids who want to ride alongside parents and peers\nFamily rides, outdoor adventures and weekend trail trips\n\nFind the right fit\nThe Tract Jr. 24 is designed for riders aged 9–11 and features 24\" wheels for growing riders. Use our Kids' Bike Size Guide by clicking the tab above to find the right bike based on your child's height and age.",
